  "observations": [
    "The generated60-second MP4 adds three native chapters at0/20/40seconds to the owned video/audio/subtitle fixture. Native C API descriptions retain the literal Unicode name; selected chapters2/1/0 report40/20/0seconds plus the established1microsecond clock origin while remaining paused. Release reaches stopped4; all guards pass.",
    "Ordinary GUI329: Chapters tile opens the genuine list; offsets0/20/40and literal Middle <b>\u00e4\u00f6</b> display correctly. Double-click seeks the blue20-second frame, mouse-select/Return seeks green40, and mouse-select/Space seeks red0 while paused. Playing selection retains playback and the clock advances.",
    "The playing run reaches EOF before the later Pause action and automatically advances to plain Show.S01E02. Its chapter rows clear and the tile disables. Pause settles on the plain source; Previous starts chaptered playback and restores all three rows. No manual Next click, bounded seek latency or preserved pause across Previous is claimed.",
    "A timeline click exposes the old tooltip formatting defect: its accessibility string contains literal tags, but the screenshot renders Middle \u00e4\u00f6 with bold formatting. ToolTipExt now exposes its text-format alias; PointingTooltip selects PlainText. Other ToolTipExt defaults are retained.",
    "Actual production tooltip Qt text layout compared with independent literal Text: two pass/three expected failures before, five pass after, no messages. This checks tags, br-looking text, entities, ordinary text and empty text; supplied style/MainCtx dependencies do not establish ordinary popup placement.",
    "Ordinary GUI337 renders the complete literal chapter name in its timeline tooltip. Zero/ending tooltips appear inside the window near timeline edges; paused seeking produces the expected red/blue frames and selected captions. An immediate near-end capture still has the preceding red frame; the later settled capture shows the blue ending frame and last cue. No latency bound or initial-frame pass is inferred from the stale capture.",
    "Both completed ordinary journeys exit0/602modules/zero error diagnostics/all guards, including the new chapter fixture. The early r333 launcher exits1 for a missing final chapter-fixture result key after a normal app exit; the corrected r334 run includes and passes that check. The first tooltip component attempt retains its font-directory setup warning; the same semantic failures are reproduced cleanly after selecting the existing Inter font."
  ],
